From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:09:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the DS touch screen

hud_nds.c draws the touch screen in a game: Quake II's status bar at the
top on a dark strip, the map in the middle, following you, with the
level name, time, kills, goals and secrets, and at the bottom a cell for
each weapon with its icon and ammo, dark until you have it, and one for
the selected item. A tap on a weapon uses it, on the item uses that, on
its arrows selects the previous or next one. With the menu and while no
game runs it shows the controls over the console background. What it
shows is only redrawn when it changed, the map every fourth frame while
you move.
---
 nds/hud_nds.c | 438 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 438 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 nds/hud_nds.c

diff --git a/nds/hud_nds.c b/nds/hud_nds.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..489292e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/nds/hud_nds.c
@@ -0,0 +1,438 @@
